# V4: restored. V3 cut this from 80 lines to 27 and dropped load-bearing rules.
# ios/Godstone/.build/ alone holds ~346 MB across ~3,599 files, and a single
# `git add .` would have ingested it.

# --- build output ---
dist/
build/
.build/
.gradle/
.cxx/
captures/
local.properties
# CI evidence scratch: release-gates.yml / android-archive-only-release writes
# the resolved lightRelease dep graph + APK/AAB namelist/SHA-256/merged-manifest
# inspection here, then uploads it as a workflow artifact. It is never committed;
# gitignoring it keeps the final clean-tree (git status --porcelain) provenance
# check green after the build produces it.
artifacts/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.xcresult/
*.dex

# --- signing keys and secrets. NEVER commit. ---
*.keystore
*.jks
secrets.properties
google-services.json
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# --- large binaries, produced by scripts, never committed ---
models/
*.gguf
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# --- native dependency checkout; pinning method is still an open release gate ---
third_party/llama.cpp/

# --- Xcode: the project is GENERATED from ios/project.yml ---
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
Pods/
# xcodegen/xcodebuild writes the derived-data tree here (SYNCDIR), not under
# DerivedData/, so the rule above does not catch it. Keep it out of the repo.
ios/.xcd-derived/

# --- Kotlin/Gradle compiler caches written next to the build ---
.android/.kotlin/
android/.kotlin/

# The app currently has no external Swift package dependency graph worth locking.
# Revisit when a reviewed native-dependency pinning strategy is added.
Package.resolved

# --- simulator artefacts ---
meshsim/out/
meshsim/logs/
*.meshlog

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- verification provenance manifests (ci/provenance.py) ---
# Written by every verification job to record the clean-commit binding; emitted
# as a workflow artifact, never committed. Gitignored so the provenance step's
# own output does not dirty the tree and fail the final clean-commit check.
provenance.json
provenance-*.json

# --- editors ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --- builder live runtime journal (docs/production-readiness) ---
# Machine-owned process state, mirrored to the private evidence root outside
# the repo. Never committed. The reviewed, nonsecret evidence-index.json IS
# committed (section 25). This rule exists so the journal can never dirty the
# clean-tree provenance checks.
docs/production-readiness/.runtime-state.json

# *** THE iOS LANE'S RESULT ARTIFACT (introduced in f4c864d5). ***
# (wording RECONSTRUCTED 2026-09-19: the commit that introduced this rule also ATE its own prose -- the
#  heredoc swallowed the backticks and the text -- so no commit ever carried the original wording. THIS IS
#  A PARAPHRASE FROM f4c864d5's COMMIT MESSAGE, NOT A RECOVERY. The commit SHA is cited rather than a round
#  number because the SHA is verifiable and the round label was not.)
# `swift test` writeth NO xunit file, so its LOG is the only artifact the lane produceth -- the Android
# lanes' results live under `build/`, already ignored above. So LANE RESULTS parses this log directly
# rather than by a grep that could only print failures. *Like the Android lanes' `build/test-results/`,
# this is RUN OUTPUT and not source; the control REFUSES WHEN IT IS ABSENT, so an unrun lane is never a
# pass.*
#
# *THE EXACT COUNTS THIS CONTROL PARSES ARE NOT RESTATED HERE. They were once pasted in beside the rule
# and became a LIE: the mesh and iOS figures quoted in that paste were the INFLATED pre-correction numbers
# (sibling task directories summed into one lane), since measured down to the source census. A COMMENT THAT
# MIRRORS A MEASUREMENT GOES STALE SILENTLY; the control printeth the live figures on every run.*
ios-ui-lane.log
ios-lane.log

# *** LANE PROVENANCE SIDECARS (introduced in 74155b42). ***
# (wording RECONSTRUCTED 2026-09-19, on the same terms as the block above: paraphrase from 74155b42's own
#  commit message, because the introducing heredoc ate the original. Earlier revisions of this comment said
#  "round 697"; the measured introducer is 74155b42, so the unverifiable round label is replaced by the SHA.)
# Written by the RUNNERS, beside each artifact: `ios-lane.log.sources.sha256` and
# `android-*.sources.sha256`. THE RUNNER IS THE ONLY PARTY THAT KNOWETH WHICH TREE IT COMPILED; the control
# can only CHECK. Each digest is over content, path-sorted, and SHARED between runner and control -- the
# digest scripts IMPORT the control's own source-list definition rather than restating it, because two
# copies would drift and a digest over a different list is a different claim.
#
# LANE RESULTS refuseth an ABSENT digest (a result with no provenance cannot be dated, and an undatable
# result is not evidence about the current tree) and a DIVERGENT one (STALE -- the results never saw these
# sources). *Run output, like the Android lanes' `build/test-results/` -- and the control REFUSES WHEN
# ABSENT, so an unprovenanced result is never a pass.*
*.sources.sha256
# *** AND THE PRE-RUN DIGEST (Step 11, the mid-run-edit guard). *** *`run_ios_ui_lane.sh` taketh the source digest
# BEFORE the schemes run and writeth it to `<log>.pre.sha256`; the checker requireth it to EQUAL the post-run sidecar,
# so an edit DURING a run cannot leave a log that describeth a tree the tests never compiled.*
*.pre.sha256
